# MOONWITNESS XV — Integrated Task Crosswalk & Release Path

**DRAFT ONLY · NO REPO WRITE · NO NEW OFFICIAL IDS · Audit latest recheck SHA `7e8483e5973279572d6777532d15afc494a83f36` (initial baseline `4c6344625597d5fb479967db07d3b52a0ddc6147`) · 2026-10-26**

This is a *proposed reconciliation overlay* on `TODO.md` (29 milestones, 203 existing task IDs). This is **not a replacement execution register**, not evidence of completion, and not authorization to create issues/branches/commits. Revalidate on latest HEAD, since a local AI may be working in parallel.

## 1. Mandatory order (dependency gates, not new milestones)

1. **Integrity regression gate**: frozen install and exact-HEAD CI have **PASSED at `7e8483e`, run `40296311027`**. Do NOT reimplement the resolved lockfile fix. Recheck only after new HEAD changes (M01-03, M05-07).
2. **Boundary security**: Cockpit local API control permissions/CORS/CSRF; AI Gateway exposed unauthenticated POST + cross-provider fallback; Sentinel static credential guesses; Journey public mandates (M03-07, M21-04, M23-02). No internet/public release while unverified.
3. **Exact source/rights**: Compare Reader hardcoded rights, plus newly added `/research` reading candidate models as public REST; filter released projections rather than raw `ADMIN_WRITE` rows (M07-04, M18-01/02/06).
4. **Ontology/name decisions**: 8 II eras vs 8 editorial eras; GOD99 vs 99 chapters; current `moonql-*` packages vs outdated domain docs (M02-01/02/07, M06-03).
5. **App boundaries & functional truth**: one Dock layout + IA; HQ truthful dashboard and real research reviewer; Cockpit canonical React client; ARSY rename with tests only after foundation (M19-03, M20-01/02, M28).
6. **Visual/behavior QA**: MoonUI tokens, status model, mobile/RTL/keyboard/screenshot; optional Moonframe adapter only after core semantics (M19-01..07).
7. **End-to-end right-sized release**: source-first Reader, one reviewed term+figure+research and consent-gated public projection + existing Radio; World/Cosmos/Journey expansions nonblocking (M18, M22, M27).

